<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">George Clifford, 3rd Earl of Cumberland</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1558">1558</a>–<a href="/years/1605">1605</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">George Clifford, 3rd Earl of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cumberland">Cumberland</a> (1558–1605), was an English courtier, naval commander and privateer who financed a dozen expeditions against Spanish shipping and colonies. In 1598 he captured San Juan in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puerto-rico">Puerto Rico</a>, taking El Morro after a siege, and planned to hold the island, but dysentery killed hundreds of his men and he withdrew after a few months. He was also champion at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elizabeth-i">Elizabeth I</a>'s tournaments.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/george-clifford-3rd-earl-of-cumberland.jpg" alt="George Clifford, 3rd Earl of Cumberland" width="320" height="404" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: After Nicholas Hilliard (died 1619) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:George_Clifford_3rd_Earl_of_Cumberland_after_Nicholas_Hilliard.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
